</head>
<body>
<div class="rxc-shell top" role="banner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12"/></svg>RadicalxChange</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="here">Wentworth on migration</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="right">
      <span class="status"><i></i><span data-k="status">Preliminary results, data to 4:45am AEDT, 20 November 2026</span></span>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Wentworth%20migration%20results">Contact the team</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1><span class="ln">Wentworth wants</span><span class="ln"><span class="box">joined-up planning</span></span><span class="ln">for migration</span></h1>
        <p class="sub intro" data-k="intro">Multiculturalism is central to Australia’s story, identity and future. As debate over migration levels and settings continues, this process offers a more nuanced, participatory way for communities to give feedback on immigration policy.</p>
        <p class="sub" data-k="herosub">People here disagree about how many should come and who should be chosen. But all three groups want state and federal planning aligned, and a much more transparent system. When people voted on priorities, planning migration with housing and infrastructure came first.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Wentworth said</a><a class="btn line" href="#priorities">The changes people want most</a></div>
        <p class="turnout" data-k="turnout">Since 2 November 2026 · 154 people have taken part · 131 in a group</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="glabels" role="list" aria-label="The three groups">
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-1" style="--gc:var(--g1)"><small data-k="hl1n">Group 1 · 84 people</small><b><span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="1">Migration is good for us; do more for refugees.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-2" style="--gc:var(--g2)"><small data-k="hl2n">Group 2 · 32 people</small><b><span data-gname="2">Fewer, but flexible</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="2">Housing and English first, but open to care workers.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-3" style="--gc:var(--g3)"><small data-k="hl3n">Group 3 · 15 people</small><b><span data-gname="3">Fewer, chosen more carefully</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="3">Tie migration to local housing and jobs.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <a class="sticker" href="#agree" aria-label="More than 9 in 10 in all three groups want state and federal planning aligned. See what they agree on."><div aria-hidden="true" data-k="sticker"><span>More than</span><b>9 in 10</b><span>in all three groups want state and federal planning aligned</span></div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Most people fit into one of three groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person, placed by how they voted. People who voted alike sit close together, so the higher the pile, the more people voted that way.</p>
      <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 1000 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-desc"><desc id="map-desc">131 people placed along the main divide in the votes. Group 1, Migration works, 84 people, sits to the left in a high pile. Group 2, Fewer, but flexible, 32 people, sits to the right of it, in a lower pile. Group 3, Fewer, chosen more carefully, 15 people, is spread thinly at the far right.</desc></svg>
      <div class="map-foot">
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint"><span class="h-fine">Hover over a dot to see how that person voted.</span><span class="h-touch">Tap the map or press “Show me someone” to see how one person voted.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one" id="group-1">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g1f">2<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g1"></i><span>Group 1: <span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></span></b><span data-k="g1n">84 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols" data-k="card1">
          <div class="qbox"><q>As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren't so lucky, even when it costs us.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>23%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>7%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>As a wealthy country we have a responsibility to support genuine refugees far more than we currently do.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>77%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>27%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>7%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>83%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>34%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>0%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two" id="group-2">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g2f">1<small> in </small>4</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g2"></i><span>Group 2: <span data-gname="2">Fewer, but flexible</span></span></b><span data-k="g2n">32 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">Where they stand</p>
        <div class="gcols two" data-k="card2">
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g1"></i><span>Like Group 1 · <span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></span></p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Australia needs more than top professionals. We rely on aged care and disability workers from overseas, so there should be a real visa pathway for them even though the pay is low.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>85%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>33%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Migration is essential to ensure the sustainability of the healthcare workforce in Australia</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>76%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>92%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>13%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g3"></i><span>Like Group 3 · <span data-gname="3">Fewer, chosen more carefully</span></span></p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Speaking English should be a prerequisite for coming to Australia, not a skill you acquire here (unless talking about humanitarian visa)</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>97%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>22%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>93%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Housing supply needs to be addressed for those that are already here before continuing to bring in large numbers of immigrants.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>86%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>27%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>93%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="gcol wide"><p class="side">More than both other groups</p>
            <div class="qbox wide"><q>When places are limited, people who can work and contribute economically should take priority over family reunion.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>83%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>40%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>67%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard three" id="group-3">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g3f">1<small> in </small>9</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g3"></i><span>Group 3: <span data-gname="3">Fewer, chosen more carefully</span></span></b><span data-k="g3n">15 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols" data-k="card3">
          <div class="qbox"><q>Tie all migration and degrees to local housing and jobs, while rapid AI training upskills domestic workers across both cities and regions</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>69%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(13 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>23%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>25%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>The culture of my community is changing faster than people can adjust, and it's fair to worry about that.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>87%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>13%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>45%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>When discussing migration, I care much more really about infrastructure, housing, and cost-of-living than any other aspect of the problem.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>82%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(11 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>28%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>40%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note" data-k="caveat">The people who joined in aren’t a random sample, so these groups describe who took part, not all of Wentworth. 23 people voted on too few statements to be placed in a group.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block deep" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head side">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
      <p class="head-line" data-k="agreelead">At least 7 in 10 people in every group agreed with 16 statements. Here are five of them, each beside a related statement the groups disagree on.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
    <details class="all">
      <summary data-k="foldsum">See all 16 statements all three groups agreed with</summary>
      <ol class="all-list" id="all"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap" data-k="qvcap">At a community session on 2 November, 54 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding" data-k="finding">In the conversation, most people in every group agreed with two of the top six.</p>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t" data-k="no-t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s" data-k="no-s">26 people opposed it and 12 backed it. Most of the opposition was mild, with one or two votes each.</p></div>
      <div><div class="tally"><p class="big" data-k="no-net">−13<span>net votes</span></p></div></div>
    </div>
